# Next.js — project structure

Canonical tree (greenfield or when placing **new** files). Do not invent a second layout.

```
app/                      # App Router only — routes, layouts, pages
  (marketing)/            # optional route groups
  api/                    # only if this repo uses Next Route Handlers
  <feature>/
    page.tsx              # thin: compose components + load data
    layout.tsx            # optional
    loading.tsx / error.tsx  # when useful
    _components/          # feature-only UI (not shared)
components/               # shared UI reused by 2+ features
  ui/                     # primitives (Button, Modal) if the project uses them
lib/                      # pure helpers, api clients, config — no React components
  api/                    # fetch wrappers / typed clients
hooks/                    # shared React hooks (optional; or lib/hooks)
types/                    # shared TS types/interfaces (optional; or next to feature)
public/                   # static assets only
```

## Placement rules

| Kind | Put it in |
|------|-----------|
| Route / URL | `app/**/page.tsx` (or `route.ts` for handlers) |
| Feature-only UI | `app/<feature>/_components/` |
| Shared UI | `components/` |
| Data fetching helpers | `lib/api/` |
| Shared hooks | `hooks/` or `lib/hooks/` |
| Env/config accessors | `lib/` |

## Hard rules

- `page.tsx` **orchestrates** — no large inline markup or fat state machines. Extract to `_components/` or `components/`.
- No business SQL or Express routes inside `app/` unless the project already uses Route Handlers for that.
- Do not create `pages/` (Pages Router) in an App Router project.
- Soft ~150 lines per `.tsx` — split before growing (see `react-components.mdc`).
- `'use client'` only on leaves that need the browser; keep Server Components by default.
